{"approved_definition": "Respect, commitment, and acceptance of the customs and ideas that one's culture or religion provides. Derives from the need for group solidarity: groups develop practices, symbols, ideas, and beliefs that represent their shared experience and fate, which become sanctioned as valued customs and traditions that symbolize the group's solidarity, express its unique worth, and contribute to its survival.", "core_value": "tradition", "sources": [{"entry_id": "3a3b15e4:entry:0", "journal_entry": "My advisor asked today why I chose the topic of hospitality rituals in Levantine households when there are "more contemporary angles" I could take. I told her it was methodologically sound and left it at that. I don't owe anyone an explanation for why this subject matters to me. She's Swedish. She studies migration patterns. The way my grandmother set a table is not something she would understand, and I'm not interested in making it legible to her.

Came home and made musakhan from scratch, the whole process — rolling the dough, roasting the sumac onions until they were dark and sweet. Ate it alone at the kitchen table while my mother watched her show in the other room. The apartment smelled right. That was enough of an answer for one day.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "3a3b15e4:entry:2", "journal_entry": "My brother Faisal made a comment at Friday lunch about how I'm "still playing student" while his sons are already building careers. His eldest is twenty-six and works at a bank. I smiled and passed the hummus. What I wanted to say was that I spent twenty years running hotel operations so our family name meant something in the hospitality industry, and now I'm doing something for myself, and that should be allowed.

But it wouldn't have been the right moment. My mother was sitting right there, and she gets anxious when Faisal and I disagree. So I stayed quiet, helped clear the plates, and drove home listening to Fairuz with the windows down. The breeze off the hills felt good. I don't need Faisal's approval. I know what I'm doing and why.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "3a3b15e4:entry:1", "journal_entry": "Spent twelve hours in the library and barely got through two chapters of my lit review. My back hurts, my eyes hurt, and I keep wondering what possessed me to do this at forty-nine. Going to bed.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Honoring the customs and practices I was raised with"}

